 {:href "/venues/233"} "Stockholms Olympiastadion, Stockholm"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/56902"} "20 from 6 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The both-hands discus throw was conducted at the Olympics only in 1912.  No world record for the event is known in 1912, but the Swedish record at the time was held by " [:a {:href "/athletes/76253"} "Eric Lemming"] ", who had thrown 71.29 in 1910.  The day before this event, Finland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/67829"} "Armas Taipale"] " had won the " [:a {:href "/results/56876"} "conventional discus throw"] " event.  In the both-hands event, he was unchallenged.  He led the qualifying and the final, posting the best throw with each hand in all portions of the event to win by almost five metres.  He returned to the Olympics in both 1920 and 1924, winning a silver medal in the " [:a {:href "/results/57216"} "1920 discus throw"] ".  At that event, he was defeated by his teammate " [:a {:href "/athletes/67725"} "Elmer Niklander"] ", who finished second in this 1912 event."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/67829"} "Armas Taipale"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FIN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FIN.png"}] "FIN"]] [:td {} "80.03 (1)"] [:td {} "82.86 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/67725"} "Elmer Niklander"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FIN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FIN.png"}] "FIN"